 | Atmosphere editor (2026-10-24) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+2 tests in `world/atmos.rs`, +1 in `options.rs`) | Pause menu > the pixel sun at its bottom right corner (not on the death screen). A panel down the left; the world stays undimmed beside it and follows every slider at once. `<` name `>` or the list picks the biome (opens on the one under the player, a gold dot marks edited ones); tabs Sky / Fog / Clouds / Haze / Stars hold all 21 values of `world::atmos`'s look (colour as red / green / blue sliders with a swatch and hex code, plus gradient, fog density, cloud cover and speed, haze strength, star brightness). `Reset biome` / `Reset all`. Edited biomes are saved as `atmos_<n>:` lines of options.txt (n = the biome's place in `atmos::ALL`) when a slider is let go. Colours are the biome's noon colours: night and rain still follow the vanilla curves. Not there: a time-of-day / weather preview, copy and paste of a look, an in-world list of the biome under the cursor. |
 | Shoulder-surf view (2026-10-24) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+8 tests in `render/shoulder.rs`, the view-button test rewritten in `touch_ui.rs`); `python3 tools/shoulder_proto.py` (the twin of the maths) passes | `render/shoulder.rs`: a cinematic over-the-shoulder camera, the view button's second tap (first person -> third -> shoulder surf). NOT b1.7.3. Glides in from the vanilla third-person place (4 blocks behind the eye, no dolly out from the head, no field-of-view whip), a pivot a shoulder to the right that follows through springs (slower on xz than y), crosshair convergence (the camera turns to the point the eye's pick ray hits, rack-focused), automatic shoulder swap at a wall, 5-ray collision (instant in, eased out), bank into strafes and turns, landing dip / jump lift / hit kick on under-damped springs, sneak tuck, zoom = aiming shot, sprint pull-back, hand-held sway. See the rendering changelog. |
 | Grazing + idle behaviours (2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run; **NOT b1.7.3** (+4 tests in `world/mobs.rs`, +1 in `render/items.rs`; run `cargo test --lib mobs items` first) | Part of the smart animals switch (`animalAi`, on by default; `animalAi:false` gives the b1.7.3 AI back byte for byte). `Mob::idle`: a calm pig, cow, sheep or hen pauses to do something instead of only standing: a cow or sheep on grass **grazes** (3 to 8 s), a pig **roots** on grass or dirt (2 to 5 s), a hen **pecks** (1 to 2 s), and a cow, sheep or pig now and then **rests** (8 to 20 s). Eating and resting stay put, do not turn, and end when a person comes within 4 blocks or the animal is hit. Each wander walk has its own gait (a stroll at 0.6 to 1.0 x the walk, a hen sometimes dashes at 1.5 x). The head is drawn dipped to the ground (`Mob::head`, `Mob::munch`, `render/items.rs::head_dip`) with a chew or a quick peck. The grass is not eaten and nothing lies down. See the gameplay changelog. |
-| Immersive pack (The Forest style, 2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+4 tests in `world/pack.rs`, `menu.rs` flow test extended); **NOT b1.7.3** | `world/pack.rs` + `lib.rs` + `render/items.rs` + `menu.rs`: with the world's **Immersive Pack** switch on (Create World screen, saved as the 4th line of `<world>/info`; worlds made before it keep the panel), the inventory button no longer opens the inventory: it spreads a cloth on the flat ground under the crosshair (needs a full block under 9 samples of a 2.0 x 1.6 footprint, nothing but air or plants on it; else a message). The cloth unrolls in the world (0.9 s, a roll that shrinks as it travels), then the screen opens as the cloth: items lie in zones by category (tools & gear, food, materials, other), each at its own size, shrunk together when a zone is crowded; the crafting mat (2 x 2), worn armor and the quick-select row (hotbar) have fixed places. Same `SlotId`s and `Screen::click` as the panel, so crafting, armor, spread-drag, place-one and shift-click work unchanged. Closing, walking 6.5 blocks off or losing the ground rolls it up. A workbench, furnace and chest keep their own panels. Switch off = the old panel. See the gameplay changelog. |
+| Immersive pack (The Forest style, 2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+5 tests in `world/pack.rs`, `menu.rs` flow test extended, carry check in `render/player.rs`); **NOT b1.7.3** | `world/pack.rs` + `lib.rs` + `render/items.rs` + `menu.rs`: with the world's **Immersive Pack** switch on (Create World screen, saved as the 4th line of `<world>/info`; worlds made before it keep the panel), the inventory button no longer opens the inventory: the player takes the pack in both hands (it rises from below, the held item is hidden) and the cloth shows on the flat ground under the crosshair, lime where it fits and red where it does not (needs a full block under 9 samples of a 2.0 x 1.6 footprint, nothing but air or plants on it); a tap, like placing a block, spreads it there (on a red one only a message shows), the button again puts the pack away. The cloth unrolls in the world (0.9 s, a roll that shrinks as it travels), then the screen opens as the cloth: items lie in zones by category (tools & gear, food, materials, other), each at its own size, shrunk together when a zone is crowded; the crafting mat (2 x 2), worn armor and the quick-select row (hotbar) have fixed places. Same `SlotId`s and `Screen::click` as the panel, so crafting, armor, spread-drag, place-one and shift-click work unchanged. Closing, walking 6.5 blocks off or losing the ground rolls it up. A workbench, furnace and chest keep their own panels. Switch off = the old panel. See the gameplay changelog. |
 | M14                  | pending | Menus (part 1: title, world list, create world; see above), options, chat, real mob models, player armor: see [`roadmap/gameplay.md`](roadmap/gameplay.md). M10 multiplayer and M13 optimization are out of scope on purpose. |
 
